/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186560935 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561009 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162654" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561009 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561009 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s)=⟨\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1},\\,8s,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+2)⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561009 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6a136627-eda2-5d29-b505-8b7058c4663c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561009 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $8s$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+2)$ is $s\\in (-2,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/39/39aa3fde0371988849572ce6f92a7e9994e4756db4aafd6f82dc7c86aa321dc1.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s)$ is $s\\in (-2,\\infty ).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561016 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186560916 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561016 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161527" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561016 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561016 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=⟨5t,\\,\\frac{1}{(t+2)^{2}},\\,{e}^{t}+t⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561016 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "72c1cee2-c377-54c5-9063-216281f970a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561016 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $5t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\frac{1}{(t+2)^{2}}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (-2,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component ${e}^{t}+t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/b5/b50ca0dfe2d2fa5a56edd03e9e4817751f821d610faba2e2dd3eb07982157a4a.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (-2,\\infty ).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561029 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186560892 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561029 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161534" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561029 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561029 #edb/ref 1071 "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡t\\,i+{e}^{-{t}^{2}}\\,j+(t-1)^{3}\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\bbox[5pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561029 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8fca9eb0-e6f5-519c-a32f-bb2e9feb0354" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561029 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the $1$st component $\\operatorname{csc}⁡t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ $t\\ne n\\pi ,$  where $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the $2$nd component  ${e}^{-{t}^{2}}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the $3$rd component $(t-1)^{3}$ is  $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561061 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186560967 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561061 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162680" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561061 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561061 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=({t}^{2}+t)\\,i+\\frac{1}{2+2t}\\,j+\\sqrt{2-t}\\,k.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561061 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f4e2f465-8077-58ed-9a98-b0019bd19799" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561061 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component ${t}^{2}+t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\frac{1}{2+2t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (-1,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $\\sqrt{2-t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,2].$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/61/61138db6d0965f64d225d694f90e237955db1e5adfb67cfbf6adfae82520f3aa.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (-1,2].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
